REVIEW UPDATE: The original behavior described below was rejected and superseded by commit ba4f3ef69. It skipped checksum-corrupt frames, which can hide an end-seed marker or a partial line; it is not the final behavior.

Final branch head: ba4f3ef69 (fix/wip-sessions-frame-tail), two commits ahead, clean, no push.
The reader now stops on all decoder errors and malformed headers. A failed dsh read keeps the last successful summary and calls; without one it returns no partial data. Summary cache version 27 and calls-v16 invalidate results from the earlier skip. Incomplete frames still wait for more data. A modified size or timestamp prompts a retry, with the existing sampled-prefix tail validation; same metadata or an unsampled rewrite may leave older cached data.

Red against 1e7183e: TestCorruptFrameDoesNotExposeLineContinuation emitted suffix alone; TestDshCorruptSeedCacheRepair counted 106 input tokens (99 inherited + 7 own). Exit 1. A first version of the cache test timed out because the test left the global cache nil while calling refresh; its fixture was corrected to initialize the cache. This was test setup, not a production timeout.
Green against ba4f3ef69 tree: the focused tests passed through the real summary refresh and calls cache, including repair and read again; go test -tags nogui ./internal/sessions -count=1 passed (5.944s); focused go test -race -tags nogui passed (2.129s); go build ./... and go vet ./... exited 0; gofmt -l and git diff --check clean. gopls unavailable; full repository suite and cross-platform tests not run.

Remaining limit: no safe automatic resynchronization across any corrupt frame or malformed header. Later data remains inaccessible until the source is repaired and the change is detected; same-size, same-time repair may not be noticed. Existing cached successful state may remain visible until a successful reread. No push.

