scanFrames is called by parseDsh and readDshCalls; both persist tails only on nil errors. A complete frame whose decoder reports a checksum mismatch can be passed at its parsed end when no prior incomplete line or skip depends on it; both real callers are exercised by a test and retain the later frame. Malformed frame headers and all other decoder errors are returned, stopping safely; callers discard the tail and retry from the start on a later read. Partial frames and partial magic are retained for future appends.

