Limit: malformed headers have no trustworthy end, and searching for frame magic can mistake compressed or raw payload for an independent frame. An incomplete outer raw block can contain a whole decodable zstd frame as data. The same prefix can represent a corrupted length followed by a valid frame. Therefore malformed headers stop without recovering later frames, as do non-checksum decoding errors (including unknown dictionaries and decoder limits) and corrupt frames crossing an unfinished line. No claim of universal recovery. Content inside a checksum-failed frame cannot be recovered; the fix skips that frame only at a known parsed boundary.

